Description: Allow LAN peers in Kad so a fully private aMule Kad mesh can route.
 aMule's IsGoodIPPort() hardcodes IsGoodIP(ip, true), which rejects every
 RFC1918 / LAN address for Kad regardless of the FilterLanIPs preference. That
 makes a private, air-gapped Kad mesh impossible: nodes never add each other to
 their routing tables. Passing filterLAN=false lets LAN peers be added.
 .
 IsLanIP() itself is deliberately left intact: aMule's LAN mode
 (CKademlia::IsRunningInLANMode + CRoutingZone::HasOnlyLANNodes) relies on it to
 detect an all-LAN routing table and switch to the non-firewalled "home LAN"
 behaviour, which is exactly what an isolated interop mesh needs. Patching
 IsLanIP instead would defeat LAN mode and leave every node firewalled.
 .
 This relaxes a deployment guard only; no Kad protocol/wire logic is changed, so
 captured datagrams remain genuine aMule output. For private interop evidence
 capture exclusively.
Author: rmule interop harness
Forwarded: not-needed
--- a/src/NetworkFunctions.h
+++ b/src/NetworkFunctions.h
@@ -116,7 +116,9 @@ bool IsGoodIP( uint32 IP, bool filterLAN ) throw();

 inline bool IsGoodIPPort(uint32 nIP, uint16 nPort) throw()
 {
-	return IsGoodIP(nIP, true) && nPort!=0;
+	// rmule interop patch: allow LAN peers so a private aMule Kad mesh can route
+	// and enter LAN mode (IsLanIP stays intact for LAN-mode detection).
+	return IsGoodIP(nIP, false) && nPort!=0;
 }

 #define HIGHEST_LOWID_ED2K_KAD		16777216
